course: dictionary
lesson: 12022
title: Chivvy: nagging and chasing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chivvy is an everyday British word, and it is informal, so you will hear it in chatty speech more than in formal writing. It means to keep telling someone to hurry up, in an annoying way. «Mum had to chivvy me to get my shoes on before school.» The clues are hurry up and annoying: Mum was getting impatient with you.
explain: The word can also mean to chase or drive animals along. «The farmer's dog chivvied the sheep into the pen.» Chivvy is often followed by a small word such as along, into or out of. Those little words show where the hurrying or chasing goes, so «chivvy along» and «chivvy into» can mean slightly different things.
explain: Look at the sentence around the word to decide which meaning fits. In «The teacher chivvied the class into line», the children are being hurried and moved, so it is about getting people to move. In older stories, such as The Wind in the Willows, animals are chivvied and chased by others. Swap in a simpler meaning, like hurry or chase, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Chivvy is a verb: chivvy, chivvies, chivvied, chivvying.
fact: Chivvy can also be spelt chivy.
fact: «Chivvy» means to keep telling someone to hurry up, in an annoying way.
fact: «Chivvy» can also mean to chase or hunt someone, or drive animals along.
fact: Chivvy is mainly British and informal, so it is a chatty word rather than a formal one.
exercise: «Dad had to chivvy us to get in the car.» What does chivvy mean here? | To paint the car bright red | To hug us warmly | *To keep telling us to hurry up, in an annoying way | To ask us a quiet question
exercise: «The sheepdog chivvied the lambs back into the field.» What is the sheepdog doing? | Counting the sheep | *Driving the lambs along and back into the field | Singing to the lambs | Sleeping under the gate
exercise: In «Mum chivvied the twins out of bed», which word shows that chivvy happened in the past? | twins | *chivvied | Mum | bed
test: Ravi says chivvy is a posh word for a hug. What does it really mean? | To read a book quietly | To cuddle someone gently | To sing a song together | *To keep telling someone to hurry up, in an annoying way
test: «The ducks were chivvied off the path by the noisy dog.» What does this suggest the dog did? | Fed them bread | Taught them to swim | Gave the ducks a gift | *Chased them away from the path
exam: «The coach chivvied the team into the changing room.» Which meaning fits best? | Gave them a prize | Left them alone to rest | Sang them a song to calm them | *Hurried them along and pushed them to move
